failure (for example, `tests/pallas/pallas_test.py::PallasCallInterpretTest::test_dot_precision10` ) on one of AMD cards, when I noticed something strange: while the test is using Pallas interpret mode (the interpret flag is set indeed), which has to run strictly on CPU, the execution seems to follow full GPU compilation route. Here's a backtrace of a function call that is supposed to run for a GPU only:\n\n<img width=\"684\" height=\"443\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c2d834d5-189c-48de-a75e-e4e8b3c51fc5\" />\n\nWhat is even more strange, is that the same NON-interpret test ( `tests/pallas/pallas_test.py::PallasCallTest::test_dot_precision10` ) doesn't use that execution path at all, but some other (and it doesn't fail due to not being blocked by that `IsSupportedDotAlgorithmOnGpu()` gate keeper function )\n\nIs this an expected behavior of Pallas Interpret and regular modes? Shouldn't interpret mode run on the CPU backend instead of GPU? Can you please help explain how is it supposed to work?\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\nPython 3.10.12\nJAX 0.6.0 (AMD/ROCm specific)\n","closed_at":"2025-07-16T08:16:58Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208770786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Arech8","id":208770786,"login":"Arech8","node_id":"U_kgDODHGW4g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arech8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github